  { number := 230, text := "### 6.3 Product claims that are not ready for use" },
  { number := 231, text := "" },
  { number := 232, text := "1. This document specifies Continuous Integration and stack consistency. The work is ongoing and is not ready for use. It MUST NOT be read as claiming that Continuous Integration never started or does not exist." },
  { number := 233, text := "2. Byte identity of Slake emit (Clause 3.10 and Clause 4.7) is a requirement on a conforming Systems Lean and Slake product. This document does not claim that match already holds. The match is not claimed done. Slake work is ongoing and is not ready for use. Companion Lean SHALL NOT treat emit equal to `ELF` as a proved identity. Treating byte identity of emit as already true is Cons False in the CI proofs module. Remaining work is the Systems Lean and Slake product, not a proved identity in this repository." },
  { number := 234, text := "3. The SSSSS and beastdb reality check (Clause 3.11 and Clause 4.8) is a requirement on a conforming SSSSS and beastdb stack. SSSSS and beastdb are ongoing and not ready for use. Do not write that they never started or do not exist. This document does not claim the check is done. Treating that check as done is Cons False in the CI proofs module. Remaining work is the SSSSS and beastdb product stack, then an honest update of that claim only when the operator says the check is done." },
  { number := 235, text := "4. A GitHub Actions workflow that runs this repository's named gate is not a claim that a general Continuous Integration product is shipped." },
  { number := 236, text := "5. Clause 4 states requirements on authors, agents, this specifications repository, and product trees that claim this specification. This document does not claim those requirements are already met by every session or every tree." },
  { number := 237, text := "" },
  { number := 238, text := "### 6.4 fargo has no assigned specification number, so this document states no fargo process" },
  { number := 239, text := "" },
  { number := 240, text := "1. Rust SHALL be elevated with fargo (Clause 4.9). fargo has no assigned specification number, so this document does not state a fargo process. This document does not create a numbered file for fargo. This document MUST NOT steal 0005, 0006, or 0007 for fargo." },
  { number := 241, text := "2. fargo has no numbered specification and no assigned number. This document does not invent a numbered file for fargo. `0003_beastdb.md` still names fargo as the interoperability path; that is a requirement on a future product, not a claim that fargo is specified here." },
  { number := 242, text := "" },
  { number := 243, text := "### 6.5 Informative items this document names" },
  { number := 244, text := "" },
  { number := 245, text := "1. Formal Vibefication is specified in `0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`. The research pages cited by that document and by `0002_Systems_Lean.md` are not Clause 12 pins of this document." },
  { number := 246, text := "2. CATE is specified in `0005_CATE.md`. CATE is not this specification." },
  { number := 247, text := "3. RSI is specified in `0006_RSI.md`. RSI is not this specification." },
  { number := 248, text := "4. Ahead of time emission may be abbreviated `AOT` after it is defined. That abbreviation is not a license to write leftover unstack." },
  { number := 249, text := "" },
  { number := 250, text := "## 7. Changelog" },
  { number := 251, text := "" },
  { number := 252, text := "### 0.1.0 - 20260831" },
  { number := 253, text := "" },
  { number := 254, text := "Current version line is 0.1.0 by operator order. Changelog history records that a 1.0.0 line existed. Byte identity stays required, is not claimed true, and a `FastC` mark does not waive it. This same 0.1.0 line records that the reference side of delta reconciliation is the major compilers, that CompCert `ccomp`, `CompCertTSO`, gcc, LLVM, and `cc` are in that set, and that being a reference target does not satisfy Clause 4.2 item 6 of `0002_Systems_Lean.md`." },
  { number := 255, text := "" },
  { number := 256, text := "### 1.0.0 - 20260825" },
  { number := 257, text := "" },
  { number := 258, text := "First publication of Continuous Integration and stack consistency as numbered specification 0007 with file name `0007_CI.md`. Requires the named gate green before commit and before push, with this repository's gate `nix flake check \"path:$PWD\" --print-build-logs`. Requires commits signed by the human operator. Forbids agents from creating commit objects. Names one exception only for a product that keeps two source trees, Grok Build source people can read and a distinct Open Source version that is published, when that product's residual names the unsigned history or the history signed with a different key. Records that pre-commit may run the gate and is not a substitute for the operator signature." },
  { number := 259, text := "" },
  { number := 260, text := "This 1.0.0 keeps numbered markdown, Lean spec encodings, Lean proofs, and product implementation distinct in this specifications repository (Formal Vibefication as specified in `0008_Formal_Vibefication.md`). It records that Systems Lean product trees unify those three in one typed language and then Slake emits ahead of time freestanding C and optional LLVM IR. It requires byte identity of emit for a conforming Systems Lean and Slake product and records that the match is not claimed done. It requires the SSSSS and beastdb reality check for that stack and records that the check is not claimed done. It names fargo as the way to elevate Rust and records that fargo has no assigned specification number, so this document states no fargo process." },
  { number := 261, text := "" },
  { number := 262, text := "This 1.0.0 also records: CATE is specification 0005; RSI is specification 0006; fargo has no assigned specification number; SSSP has no assigned specification number, and this document does not create a numbered file for SSSP; Carbonado has no assigned number; this document does not claim that a conforming Continuous Integration product exists." },
  { number := 263, text := "" },
